"challenge_content": "Does the successful passage of stool during digital rectal exam directly challenge the possibility of pyloric stenosis or duodenal atresia as the cause of obstruction?"}, "B4": {"confirm_status": "deferred", "challenge_status": "covered", "confirm_content": null, "challenge_content": "Does the digital rectal exam result (successful stool/gas passage) definitively rule out intestinal malrotation with volvulus as a life-threatening alternative?"}}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 1, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the combination of Down syndrome stigmata and neonatal presentation with bilious vomiting justify higher suspicion for genetic syndrome-related mechanical obstruction?", "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the combination of Down syndrome stigmata and neonatal presentation with bilious vomiting justify higher suspicion for genetic syndrome-related mechanical obstruction?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}, "result_summary": "Bilious vomiting raises concern for mechanical obstruction, while Down syndrome features (linked to genetic syndromes) moderately support mechanical causes like duodenal atresia over functional disorders (B2).", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "weak_against", "B2": "moderate_for", "B3": "moderate_for", "B4": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of prenatal testing despite Down syndrome risk features make pre-duodenal malrotation less likely in this 37-week gestation newborn?", "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the absence of prenatal testing despite Down syndrome risk features make pre-duodenal malrotation less likely in this 37-week gestation newborn?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}, "result_summary": "Absence of prenatal polyhydramnios (which could detect duodenal atresia or malrotation) reduces the probability of known anatomical defects. This slightly weakens B3 (pre-duodenal/pyloric atresia/stenosis) compared to other mechanical causes.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "weak_against", "B4": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the firm abdomen with hypoactive bowel sounds but partial passage of stool via digital rectal exam contradict congenital aganglionic bowel as the primary diagnosis?", "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the firm abdomen with hypoactive bowel sounds but partial passage of stool via digital rectal exam contradict congenital aganglionic bowel as the primary diagnosis?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}, "result_summary": "Partial stool passage doesn't fully exclude mechanical obstruction (e.g., incomplete atresia or proximal obstruction allowing distal gas passage), but reduces the likelihood of distal mechanical causes in B2 and B3.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "moderate_for", "B2": "moderate_against", "B3": "moderate_against", "B4": "weak_against"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 4, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does effective passage of stool during digital rectal exam definitively exclude genetic syndrome-associated mechanical obstruction as the cause of symptoms?", "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does effective passage of stool during digital rectal exam definitively exclude genetic syndrome-associated mechanical obstruction as the c