cessive inheritance, chest pain, congestive heart failure, dilatation of the ventricular cavity, dyskinesia\n\nWolff-Parkinson-White Syndrome vs Congenital Long QT Syndrome with Syncope:\n  Favours first:  anxiety, blue or gray skin, cardiomyopathy, chest pain, dizziness\n  Favours second: abnormality of the ear, blurred vision, bradycardia, cardiac arrest, congestive heart failure\n\nWolff-Parkinson-White Syndrome vs Hypertrophic Obstructive Cardiomyopathy:\n  Favours first:  anxiety, blue or gray skin, dizziness, fainting, fatigue\n  Favours second: abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, arrhythmia, ascites, asymmetric septal hypertrophy, autosomal recessive inheritance\n\nWolff-Parkinson-White Syndrome vs Arrhythmogenic Right Ventricular Dysplasia:\n  Favours first:  anxiety, blue or gray skin, cardiomyopathy, dizziness, fainting\n  Favours second: autosomal recessive inheritance, bundle branch block, congestive heart failure, dilatation of the ventricular cavity, dyskinesia\n\nCongenital Long QT Syndrome with Syncope vs Hypertrophic Obstructive Cardiomyopathy:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the ear, blurred vision, bradycardia, coronary artery atherosclerosis, fainting\n  Favours second: abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, arrhythmia, ascites, asymmetric septal hypertrophy, autosomal recessive inheritance\n\nCongenital Long QT Syndrome with Syncope vs Arrhythmogenic Right Ventricular Dysplasia:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the ear, blurred vision, bradycardia, cardiac arrest, coronary artery atherosclerosis\n  Favours second: autosomal recessive inheritance, bundle branch block, chest pain, dilatation of the ventricular cavity, dyskinesia\n\nHypertrophic Obstructive Cardiomyopathy vs Arrhythmogenic Right Ventricular Dysplasia:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, arrhythmia, ascites, asymmetric septal hypertrophy, biventricular hypertrophy\n  Favours second: bundle branch block, dilatation of the ventricular cavity, dyskinesia, effort-induced polymorphic ventricular tachycardia, focal necrosis of right ventricular muscle cells\n\nNOT typically seen in Congenital Long QT Syndrome with Syncope: hearing abnormality\n\nNOT typically seen in Arrhythmogenic Right Ventricular Dysplasia: palmoplantar keratoderma\n\nRelated to Brugada Syndrome: genetic cardiac rhythm disease, heart conduction disease, syndromic disease\n\nRelated to Wolff-Parkinson-White Syndrome: heart conduction disease, mendelian disease\n\nRelated to Congenital Long QT Syndrome with Syncope: catecholaminergic polymorphic ventricular tachycardia, congenital heart disease, familial long qt syndrome\n\nRelated to Hypertrophic Obstructive Cardiomyopathy: dilated cardiomyopathy, familial dilated cardiomyopathy, familial hypertrophic cardiomyopathy\n\nRelated to Arrhythmogenic Right Ventricular Dysplasia: familial isolated arrhythmogenic ventricular dysplasia"}
