tural changes on imaging", "Tricuspid stenosis exacerbating chronic respiratory symptoms: heart function alone doesn't explain persistent airway dilation", "Metabolic/genetic disorder with multisystem involvement: delayed growth and chronic respiratory symptoms could indicate such mechanisms but require more data"], "alarm_features": ["Chronic airway dilation (bronchiectasis pattern)", "Persistent growth parameters in 25th percentile (developmental concern)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Genetic Pulmonary and Developmental Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4, "posterior": 0.40167364016736395, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Chronic airway dilation, recurrent productive cough since birth, and persistent growth delays are classic features of cystic fibrosis, which is a genetic disorder. Elevated sweat chloride (option C) is a direct diagnostic indicator for this condition.", "Subacute onset may instead suggest a chronic condition like cystic fibrosis or bronchiectasis rather than allergic airway disease. This weakens allergic (B2) but doesn't strongly support immune deficiency (B4)."], "evidence_against": ["Structural remodeling from long-standing allergic inflammation can cause airway dilation but is less likely to explain lifelong multisystem findings. This supports a chronic inflammatory (B2) rather than congenital explanation."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of consanguinity?", "Family members with similar symptoms?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Sweat chloride test", "CFTR gene panel"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Chronic Inflammatory / Allergic Airway Diseases", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3, "posterior": 0.45188284518828453, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Structural remodeling from long-standing allergic inflammation can cause airway dilation but is less likely to explain lifelong multisystem findings. This supports a chronic inflammatory (B2) rather than congenital explanation."], "evidence_against": ["Chronic airway dilation, recurrent productive cough since birth, and persistent growth delays are classic features of cystic fibrosis, which is a genetic disorder. Elevated sweat chloride (option C) is a direct diagnostic indicator for this condition.", "Subacute onset may instead suggest a chronic condition like cystic fibrosis or bronchiectasis rather than allergic airway disease. This weakens allergic (B2) but doesn't strongly support immune deficiency (B4)."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of seasonal allergy triggers?", "Response to previous inhaled steroids? (deferred in this case)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Allergy panel for IgE profiles", "Sinus CT for anatomic abnormalities"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Congenital Structural Abnormalities with Pulmonary Involvement", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.10460251046025104, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Structural remodeling from long-standing allergic inflammation can cause airway dilation but is less likely to explain lifelong multisystem findings. This supports a chronic inflammatory (B2) rather than congenital explanation."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Immune Deficiency with Chronic Infectious Sequelae", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.04184100418410042, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Normal bowel movements do not exclude cystic fibrosis as meconium ileus was likely resolved in infancy. This finding is neutral for B1 but reduces support for immune deficiency (B4) due to lack of constitutional symptoms."]}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 0, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the child's chronic airway dilation on MRI, lifelong sinus/cough symptoms, and 25th percentile growth directly associate with findings of increased chloride in sweat (option C) as seen in cystic fibrosis?", "result_summary": "Chronic airway dilation, recurrent productive cough since birth, and persistent growth delays are classic features of cystic fibrosis, which is a genetic disorder. Elevated sweat chloride (option C) is a direct diagnostic indicator for this condition.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "moderate_for", "B2": "weak_against", "B3": "neutral", "B4": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 1, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Would chronic airway dilation on MRI be better explained by structural remodeling from long-standing allergic inflammation rather than a de novo congenital issue?", "result_summary": "Structural remodeling from long-standing allergic inflammation can cause airway dilation but is less likely to explain lifelong multisystem findings. This supports a chronic inflammatory (B2) rather than congenital explanation.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "weak_against", "B2": "moderate_for", "B3": "moderate_against", "B4": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the report of 