{"case_id": "MB_17", "timestep": 2, "case_summary": "A 57-year-old man presents to the emergency department with several days of malaise, weakness, and night sweats. Today, he experienced a headache with blurry vision, thus prompting his presentation. The patient has a history of diabetes and is followed closely by an endocrinologist. Otherwise, he has lost 10 pounds over the past month. His temperature is 100°F (37.8°C), blood pressure is 122/90 mmHg, pulse is 84/min, respirations are 16/min, and oxygen saturation is 99% on room air. Physical exam is notable for a thin man but is otherwise unremarkable. His visual acuity is 20/100 in both eyes, though he says that he normally has 20/20 vision. His gait is mildly ataxic as well, but his neurological exam is otherwise nonfocal. Laboratory studies are ordered as seen below.\n\nHemoglobin: 10 g/dL\nHematocrit: 31%\nLeukocyte count: 57,500/mm^3 with 35% blasts\nPlatelet count: 109,000/mm^3\n\nSerum:\nNa+: 139 mEq/L\nCl-: 100 mEq/L\nK+: 4.1 Eq/L\nHCO3-: 22 mEq/L\nBUN: 20 mg/dL\nGlucose: 99 mg/dL\nCreatinine: 1.1 mg/dL\nCalcium: 10.0 mEq/L\n\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nOptions:\nA. Acute lymphoblastic leukemia\nB. Acute myelogenous leukemia\nC. Chronic lymphocytic leukemia\nD. Chronic myelogenous leukemia\nE. Multiple myeloma\n", "root": {"label": "Subacute Constitutional Syndrome with Hematologic Abnormalities (Anemia, Leukocytosis with Blasts, Thrombocytopenia)", "time_course": "subacute", "severity": "unspecified", "confidence": 0.75, "supporting_facts": ["Weight loss of 10 pounds in one month", "Persistent malaise, weakness, and night sweats over several days", "Low-grade fever (100°F)", "Hematologic findings: anemia (Hemoglobin 10 g/dL), leukocytosis with 35% blasts (57,500/mm³), and thrombocytopenia (109,000/mm³)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Infectious cause (e.g., sepsis): less likely due to low hemoglobin and high blast count", "Metabolic complication of diabetes: less likely given normal serum glucose, electrolytes, and systemic constitutional symptoms", "Vascular/ocular pathology: inconsistent with isolated hematologic findings and systemic context", "Neurodegenerative process: ataxia and visual changes are nonspecific and overshadowed by systemic features"], "alarm_features": ["Sustained weight loss (10% rapid decline)", "Low-grade fever with leukemic blast count ≥ 35% of circulating leukocytes", "Normocytic anemia (Hb 10 g/dL) and thrombocytopenia"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.7528517110266162, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["High blast counts with pancytopenia in peripheral blood strongly align with myeloid neoplasm. Normal creatinine and lack of lymphadenopathy reduce specificity for chronic disease or lymphoproliferative processes.", "Daily worsening of constitutional symptoms is more consistent with acute transformation (e.g., blast crisis) than chronic MPN, which typically has more prolonged progression."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Presence of bone pain or splenomegaly", "History of prior blood disorders"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow biopsy", "Cytogenetic analysis", "Flow cytometry for blast lineage"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.05703422053231938, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of B-cell lineage markers (e.g., TdT for ALL, IgM paraprotein for myeloma) and presence of blasts is pathognomonic for myeloid neoplasm, not lymphoproliferative disease."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.11406844106463876, "danger": 0.55, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Daily worsening of constitutional symptoms is more consistent with acute transformation (e.g., blast crisis) than chronic MPN, which typically has more prolonged progression."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis with Atypical Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.03802281368821293, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Inflammatory/Metabolic Syndrome with Hematologic Mimicry", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.03802281368821293, "danger": 0.25, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.41825095057034223, "posterior": 0.41825095057034223, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of prior haematological disorders (e.g., MDS, MPN, or therapy-related factors)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Flow cytometry for myeloid blast lineage (CD34, CD117, CD13, etc.)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.16730038022813692, "posterior": 0.16730038022813692, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of splenomegaly or basophilia (CML hallmark)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Cytogenetic testing for Ph+ (BCR-ABL1 translocation)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "phase_transformation", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML (t-AML)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.16730038022813692, "posterior": 0.16730038022813692, "danger": 0.65, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of prior chemotherapy/radiation (e.g., diabetes treatment with alkylating agents)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow karyotype for complex abnormalities"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "risk_context"}}, "frontier": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 0, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of 35% myeloid blasts in peripheral blood with concurrent anemia and thrombocytopenia strongly favor a myeloid neoplasm over other branches, particularly considering normal serum creatinine and no lymphadenopathy in physical exam?", "result_summary": "High blast counts with pancytopenia in peripheral blood strongly align with myeloid neoplasm. Normal creatinine and lack of lymphadenopathy reduce specificity for chronic disease or lymphoproliferative processes.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "strong_for", "B2": "weak_against", "B3": "weak_against"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 1, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Could the neurological findings (visual acuity deterioration, ataxia) be explained by plasma cell infiltration or amyloidosis (as seen in some myeloma variants), thereby supporting the lymphoproliferative/plasma cell disorder branch?", "result_summary": "Plasma cell infiltration causing acute neurological deficits is uncommon without direct evidence (e.g., lytic lesions, monoclonal protein). The findings may be early or non-specific, but lack strong linkage to plasma cell disease.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B2": "weak_for", "B3": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Could the constitutional symptoms with borderline leukocytosis be explained by inflammatory processes (e.g., MPN with concurrent infection), thereby supporting chronic neoplasm as a potential basis?", "result_summary": "While constitutional symptoms may occur in MPN with infection, the high blast percentage (35%) is more characteristic of acute myeloid leukemia than chronic MPN/MPN-related infection.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "moderate_against"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of bone pain, splenomegaly, or renal dysfunction (elevated serum creatinine) directly contradict the expected presentation of acute myeloid neoplasm?", "result_summary": "Classic acute myeloid neoplasm may present without splenomegaly or bone pain in early stages. Normal renal function weakens suspicion for severe marrow infiltration but does not directly exclude AML.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "weak_against"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 4, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the absence of B-cell chronicity markers (e.g., mature lymphocytosis pattern, monoclonal protein) and the presence of overt blasts inconsistent with a lymphoproliferative/plasma cell disorder?", "result_summary": "Lack of B-cell lineage markers (e.g., TdT for ALL, IgM paraprotein for myeloma) and presence of blasts is pathognomonic for myeloid neoplasm, not lymphoproliferative disease.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B2": "strong_against", "B3": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 1, "bundle_id": 1, "bundle_position": 5, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute progressive nature of symptoms (daily worsening vs. months) argue against a chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm in favor of an acute transformation scenario?", "result_summary": "Daily worsening of constitutional symptoms is more consistent with acute transformation (e.g., blast crisis) than chronic MPN, which typically has more prolonged progression.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "moderate_for", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "moderate_against"}}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.7528517110266162, "B2": 0.05703422053231938, "B3": 0.11406844106463876, "B4": 0.03802281368821293, "B5": 0.03802281368821293, "B1.1": 0.41825095057034223, "B1.2": 0.16730038022813692, "B1.3": 0.16730038022813692}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No universal instability markers present. Vital signs are stable (BP 122/90 mmHg, pulse 84/min, RR 16/min, O2 saturation 99% on room air). No airway compromise, severe respiratory distress, hemodynamic instability, or major neurological deficits (e.g., GCS <13 or focal motor deficit).", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Root branch (B1) has posterior >= 0.75 but unresolved dangerous child branches (B1.1 danger=0.9, B1.2 danger=0.7) remain. Further discriminators (bone marrow biopsy, flow cytometry, cytogenetics) are required to distinguish AML, CML blast crisis, or MDS/t-AML, which have distinct management implications. Depth limit not reached."}, "turn_budget_used": 1, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.83, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.41825095057034223, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_vignette": "A 57-year-old man presents to the emergency department with several days of malaise, weakness, and night sweats. Today, he experienced a headache with blurry vision, thus prompting his presentation. The patient has a history of diabetes and is followed closely by an endocrinologist. Otherwise, he has lost 10 pounds over the past month. His temperature is 100°F (37.8°C), blood pressure is 122/90 mmHg, pulse is 84/min, respirations are 16/min, and oxygen saturation is 99% on room air. Physical exam is notable for a thin man but is otherwise unremarkable. His visual acuity is 20/100 in both eyes, though he says that he normally has 20/20 vision. His gait is mildly ataxic as well, but his neurological exam is otherwise nonfocal. Laboratory studies are ordered as seen below.\n\nHemoglobin: 10 g/dL\nHematocrit: 31%\nLeukocyte count: 57,500/mm^3 with 35% blasts\nPlatelet count: 109,000/mm^3\n\nSerum:\nNa+: 139 mEq/L\nCl-: 100 mEq/L\nK+: 4.1 Eq/L\nHCO3-: 22 mEq/L\nBUN: 20 mg/dL\nGlucose: 99 mg/dL\nCreatinine: 1.1 mg/dL\nCalcium: 10.0 mEq/L", "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "static_evidence_items": [{"id": "E1", "kind": "direct", "content": "Chief complaint: several days of malaise, weakness, night sweats; today: headache with blurry vision prompting presentation", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E2", "kind": "direct", "content": "Past medical history: diabetes; monitored by endocrinologist", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E3", "kind": "direct", "content": "Weight change: 10-pound weight loss over the past month", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E4", "kind": "direct", "content": "Temperature: 100°F (37.8°C)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E5", "kind": "direct", "content": "Blood pressure: 122/90 mmHg", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E6", "kind": "direct", "content": "Pulse: 84/min", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E7", "kind": "direct", "content": "Respirations: 16/min", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E8", "kind": "direct", "content": "Oxygen saturation: 99% on room air", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E9", "kind": "direct", "content": "Physical examination finding: thin man, otherwise unremarkable", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E10", "kind": "direct", "content": "Visual acuity: 20/100 in both eyes; patient states normally has 20/20 vision", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E11", "kind": "direct", "content": "Gait: mildly ataxic; neurological exam: nonfocal", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E12", "kind": "direct", "content": "Hemoglobin: 10 g/dL (low)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E13", "kind": "direct", "content": "Hematocrit: 31% (low)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E14", "kind": "direct", "content": "Leukocyte count: 57,500/mm^3 (elevated) with 35% blasts (atypical increase)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E15", "kind": "direct", "content": "Platelet count: 109,000/mm^3 (low)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E16", "kind": "direct", "content": "Serum sodium: 139 mEq/L (normal)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E17", "kind": "direct", "content": "Serum chloride: 100 mEq/L (normal)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E18", "kind": "direct", "content": "Serum potassium: 4.1 Eq/L (normal)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E19", "kind": "direct", "content": "Serum bicarbonate: 22 mEq/L (normal)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E20", "kind": "direct", "content": "Blood urea nitrogen (BUN): 20 mg/dL (normal)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E21", "kind": "direct", "content": "Serum glucose: 99 mg/dL (normal for diabetic)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E22", "kind": "direct", "content": "Serum creatinine: 1.1 mg/dL (within normal range for diabetes)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E23", "kind": "direct", "content": "Serum calcium: 10.0 mEq/L (normal)", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Myeloproliferative disorder', 'Chronic myelogenous leukemia'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=80%, source=both]\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase) vs De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML):\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: acute myeloid leukemia, somatic mutation\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase) vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormal/excessive bleeding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase) vs Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML (t-AML):\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: myelodysplasia, somatic mutation\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis:\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormal/excessive bleeding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML (t-AML):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: myelodysplasia\n\nChronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis vs Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML (t-AML):\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormal/excessive bleeding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n  Favours second: myelodysplasia\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase): bone marrow cancer, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, not otherwise specified\n\nRelated to De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML): acute disease, acute leukemia of ambiguous lineage, acute myeloid leukemia with mutated npm1\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis: chronic myelogenous leukemia, bcr-abl1 positive\n\nRelated to Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML (t-AML): childhood myelodysplastic syndrome, chromosome 5q deletion syndrome, familial monosomy 7 syndrome\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis\n  he experienced a headache with blurry vision → seizure → Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)"}
