g Sinusoidal Thrombosis):\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n  Favours second: abducens palsy, abnormal auditory evoked potentials, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology, abnormal circulating copper concentration, abnormal cranial nerve morphology\n\nAcute Pelvic Inflammatory Disease (PID) with Rupture vs Ruptured Ectopic Pregnancy in Non-Pregnant Pelvis:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abdominal tenderness, dizziness, fainting, hypotension\n\nCholedocholithiasis with Sepsis vs Hepatic Vein Obstruction (Including Sinusoidal Thrombosis):\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity\n  Favours second: abducens palsy, abnormal auditory evoked potentials, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology, abnormal circulating copper concentration, abnormal cranial nerve morphology\n\nCholedocholithiasis with Sepsis vs Ruptured Ectopic Pregnancy in Non-Pregnant Pelvis:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n  Favours second: abdominal tenderness, dizziness, fainting, hypotension, pallor\n\nHepatic Vein Obstruction (Including Sinusoidal Thrombosis) vs Ruptured Ectopic Pregnancy in Non-Pregnant Pelvis:\n  Favours first:  abducens palsy, abnormal auditory evoked potentials, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology, abnormal circulating copper concentration, abnormal cranial nerve morphology\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abdominal tenderness, dizziness, fainting, hypotension\n\nRelated to Acute Pelvic Inflammatory Disease (PID) with Rupture: abdominal and pelvic region disorder, acute female pelvic peritonitis, female reproductive system disease\n\nRelated to Choledocholithiasis with Sepsis: bile duct disease, gallstones, genetic biliary tract disease\n\nRelated to Hepatic Vein Obstruction (Including Sinusoidal Thrombosis): hepatic vascular disease\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 23-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain → arthralgia → Acute Pelvic Inflammatory Disease (PID) with Rupture\n  A 23-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain → abdominal distention → Acute Pelvic Inflammatory Disease (PID) with Rupture\n  A 23-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain → arthralgia → Choledocholithiasis with Sepsis"}
