y deficits beyond vascular considerations", "Direct trauma: no documented abdominal injury history in hospital course"], "alarm_features": ["Post-cardiac-event elevated lipase (risk of reperfusion injury or embolic phenomena)", "Concurrent acute kidney injury with elevated creatinine", "Hypercoagulable state from hypertension/diabetes/obesity"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Acute Vascular Ischemia (Embolic/Reperfusion Related)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.24277141298417892, "posterior": 0.2180054040776222, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Absence of additional metabolic risk factors reduces support for biliary/pancreatic branch but does not exclude it given existing diabetes/obesity associations.", "The presence of atherosclerosis risk factors and subacute pancreatic/renal findings weakly supports vascular ischemic injury following acute coronary syndrome but lacks conclusive mechanistic discrimination from sequential insults."], "evidence_against": ["Concurrent pancreatic/renal injury on Day 2 following acute cardiac event shows minimal but nonzero support for critical illness multi-organ dysfunction but is insufficient to decisively displace vascular ischemia in the differential.", "Physical exam lacking new ischemia signs and unspecified procedural history slightly reduces but does not eliminate vascular embolism as a diagnostic possibility."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Did the patient undergo procedures that could release cholesterol emboli?", "Are there new signs of peripheral ischemia or visceral infarct (e.g., bowel edema on imaging)?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["CT angiography abdominal aorta and visceral vessels", "Urine microscopy for cholesterol crystals"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, 