al serum glucose, electrolytes, and systemic constitutional symptoms", "Vascular/ocular pathology: inconsistent with isolated hematologic findings and systemic context", "Neurodegenerative process: ataxia and visual changes are nonspecific and overshadowed by systemic features"], "alarm_features": ["Sustained weight loss (10% rapid decline)", "Low-grade fever with leukemic blast count ≥ 35% of circulating leukocytes", "Normocytic anemia (Hb 10 g/dL) and thrombocytopenia"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.4969199178644764, "posterior": 0.5786817556201256, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["High blast counts with pancytopenia in peripheral blood strongly align with myeloid neoplasm. Normal creatinine and lack of lymphadenopathy reduce specificity for chronic disease or lymphoproliferative processes.", "Daily worsening of constitutional symptoms is more consistent with acute transformation (e.g., blast crisis) than chronic MPN, which typically has more prolonged progression."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Presence of bone pain or splenomegaly", "History of prior blood disorders"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow biopsy", "Cytogenetic analysis", "Flow cytometry for blast lineage"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.009175714941122492, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.011469643676403116, "danger": 0.55, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis with Atypical Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.015292858235204158, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Inflammatory/Metabolic Syndrome with Hematologic Mimicry", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.015292858235204158, "danger": 0.25, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.5450374675026763, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of myeloid markers in peripheral blood suggests limited evidence for AML detection at this stage but does not definitively exclude the diagnosis due to variable expression patterns."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.016822144058724578, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML (t-AML)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.016822144058724578, "danger": 0.65, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."]}}, "frontier": [], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the rapid clinical progression (daily worsening symptoms) combined with normal renal function (Cr 1.1) argue against MDS/t-AML as root cause, since these conditions typically present with slower onset but more pronounced organ infiltration complications not evident in current lab profile?", "result_summary": "The absence of organ infiltration features (e.g., renal failure) and rapid progression contrasts with typical MDS/t-AML presentation, moderately weakening their likelihood.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.3": "moderate_against", "B1.2": "moderate_against", "B1.1": "moderate_for", "B2": "moderate_against", "B3": "moderate_against"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of specific myeloid blast lineage markers on physical exam (despite high peripheral blast count) argue against definitive diagnosis of de novo AML, since blasts should typically express myeloid antigens (CD13/33) detectable in peripheral smear in most AML cases?", "result_summary": "The lack of peripheral myeloid markers on physical exam introduces a small but non-quantitative concern for AML underdiagnosis, but does not decisively weaken its probability.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.1": "weak_against", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 4, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of splenomegaly on physical exam and normal renal function (Cr 1.1 mg/dL) contradict established CML blast crisis clinical criteria which typically exhibit massive spleen enlargement and early renal failure due to marrow fibrosis?", "result_summary": "The lack of splenomegaly and normal renal function strongly contradicts classical CML blast crisis, which would typically present with massive splenomegaly and renal impairment.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.2": "strong_against", "B3": "strong_against", "B1.1": "moderate_for", "B2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 5, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the reported history of diabetes without prior alkylating agent exposure contradict likely t-AML causation, as alkylating agents are required for t-AML development under current understanding of therapy-related leukemias?", "result_summary": "The absence of prior alkylating agent therapy directly contradicts therapy-related AML origin, strongly excluding it as a diagnosis.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.3": "strong_against", "B1.1": "moderate_for", "B1.2": "moderate_against", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 0, "bundle_size": 2, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of prior alkylating agent therapy (E2) and normal renal function (Cr 1.1, E22) strongly support de novo acute myeloid leukemia (AML) as the primary diagnosis, given their direct exclusion of therapy-related AML/t-AML and CML blast crisis as leading differentials?", "result_summary": "The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.1": "moderate_for", "B1.2": "moderate_against", "B1.3": "strong_against", "B2": "moderate_against", "B3": "moderate_against"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 1, "bundle_size": 2, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the lack of documented myeloid lineage markers on peripheral smear (implied by unremarkable physical exam) challenge the diagnosis of de novo AML, which typically presents with detectable myeloid expression (e.g., CD13/CD33) in circulating blasts?", "result_summary": "Absence of myeloid markers in peripheral blood suggests limited evidence for AML detection at this stage but does not definitively exclude the diagnosis due to variable expression patterns.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.1": "weak_against", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral"}}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.7528517110266162, "B2": 0.05703422053231938, "B3": 0.11406844106463876, "B4": 0.03802281368821293, "B5": 0.03802281368821293, "B1.1": 0.41825095057034223, "B1.2": 0.16730038022813692, "B1.3": 0.16730038022813692}, {"B1": 0.4969199178644764, "B2": 0.024640657084188906, "B3": 0.03080082135523613, "B4": 0.02053388090349076, "B5": 0.02053388090349076, "B1.1": 0.4065708418891171, "B1.2": 0.04517453798767968, "B1.3": 0.04517453798767968}, {"B1": 0.5786817556201256, "B2": 0.009175714941122492, "B3": 0.011469643676403116, "B4": 0.015292858235204158, "B5": 0.015292858235204158, "B1.1": 0.5450374675026763, "B1.2": 0.016822144058724578, "B1.3": 0.016822144058724578}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No universal instability markers present. Vital signs are stable (BP 122/90 mmHg, pulse 84/min, RR 16/min, O2 saturation 99% on room air). Mi