{"case_id": "MB_17", "timestep": 4, "case_summary": "A 57-year-old man presents to the emergency department with several days of malaise, weakness, and night sweats. Today, he experienced a headache with blurry vision, thus prompting his presentation. The patient has a history of diabetes and is followed closely by an endocrinologist. Otherwise, he has lost 10 pounds over the past month. His temperature is 100°F (37.8°C), blood pressure is 122/90 mmHg, pulse is 84/min, respirations are 16/min, and oxygen saturation is 99% on room air. Physical exam is notable for a thin man but is otherwise unremarkable. His visual acuity is 20/100 in both eyes, though he says that he normally has 20/20 vision. His gait is mildly ataxic as well, but his neurological exam is otherwise nonfocal. Laboratory studies are ordered as seen below.\n\nHemoglobin: 10 g/dL\nHematocrit: 31%\nLeukocyte count: 57,500/mm^3 with 35% blasts\nPlatelet count: 109,000/mm^3\n\nSerum:\nNa+: 139 mEq/L\nCl-: 100 mEq/L\nK+: 4.1 Eq/L\nHCO3-: 22 mEq/L\nBUN: 20 mg/dL\nGlucose: 99 mg/dL\nCreatinine: 1.1 mg/dL\nCalcium: 10.0 mEq/L\n\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nOptions:\nA. Acute lymphoblastic leukemia\nB. Acute myelogenous leukemia\nC. Chronic lymphocytic leukemia\nD. Chronic myelogenous leukemia\nE. Multiple myeloma\n", "root": {"label": "Subacute Constitutional Syndrome with Hematologic Abnormalities (Anemia, Leukocytosis with Blasts, Thrombocytopenia)", "time_course": "subacute", "severity": "unspecified", "confidence": 0.75, "supporting_facts": ["Weight loss of 10 pounds in one month", "Persistent malaise, weakness, and night sweats over several days", "Low-grade fever (100°F)", "Hematologic findings: anemia (Hemoglobin 10 g/dL), leukocytosis with 35% blasts (57,500/mm³), and thrombocytopenia (109,000/mm³)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Infectious cause (e.g., sepsis): less likely due to low hemoglobin and high blast count", "Metabolic complication of diabetes: less likely given normal serum glucose, electrolytes, and systemic constitutional symptoms", "Vascular/ocular pathology: inconsistent with isolated hematologic findings and systemic context", "Neurodegenerative process: ataxia and visual changes are nonspecific and overshadowed by systemic features"], "alarm_features": ["Sustained weight loss (10% rapid decline)", "Low-grade fever with leukemic blast count ≥ 35% of circulating leukocytes", "Normocytic anemia (Hb 10 g/dL) and thrombocytopenia"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.5786817556201256, "posterior": 0.6157421019186813, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["High blast counts with pancytopenia in peripheral blood strongly align with myeloid neoplasm. Normal creatinine and lack of lymphadenopathy reduce specificity for chronic disease or lymphoproliferative processes.", "Daily worsening of constitutional symptoms is more consistent with acute transformation (e.g., blast crisis) than chronic MPN, which typically has more prolonged progression."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Presence of bone pain or splenomegaly", "History of prior blood disorders"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow biopsy", "Cytogenetic analysis", "Flow cytometry for blast lineage"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.002845300985422573, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.003556626231778216, "danger": 0.55, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis with Atypical Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.009484336618075245, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Inflammatory/Metabolic Syndrome with Hematologic Mimicry", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.009484336618075245, "danger": 0.25, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.5450374675026763, "posterior": 0.6084391627227633, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The absence of prior alkylating agent therapy directly contradicts therapy-related AML origin, strongly excluding it as a diagnosis.", "The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."], "evidence_against": ["The lack of peripheral myeloid markers on physical exam introduces a small but non-quantitative concern for AML underdiagnosis, but does not decisively weaken its probability.", "Absence of myeloid markers in peripheral blood suggests limited evidence for AML detection at this stage but does not definitively exclude the diagnosis due to variable expression patterns."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of prior haematological disorders (e.g., MDS, MPN, or therapy-related factors)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Flow cytometry for myeloid blast lineage (CD34, CD117, CD13, etc.)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.005216385139941386, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML (t-AML)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0020865540559765546, "danger": 0.65, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."]}}, "frontier": ["B1.1", "B1.1"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of specific myeloid blast lineage markers on physical exam (despite high peripheral blast count) argue against definitive diagnosis of de novo AML, since blasts should typically express myeloid antigens (CD13/33) detectable in peripheral smear in most AML cases?", "result_summary": "The lack of peripheral myeloid markers on physical exam introduces a small but non-quantitative concern for AML underdiagnosis, but does not decisively weaken its probability.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.1": "weak_against", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 4, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of splenomegaly on physical exam and normal renal function (Cr 1.1 mg/dL) contradict established CML blast crisis clinical criteria which typically exhibit massive spleen enlargement and early renal failure due to marrow fibrosis?", "result_summary": "The lack of splenomegaly and normal renal function strongly contradicts classical CML blast crisis, which would typically present with massive splenomegaly and renal impairment.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.2": "strong_against", "B3": "strong_against", "B1.1": "moderate_for", "B2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 5, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the reported history of diabetes without prior alkylating agent exposure contradict likely t-AML causation, as alkylating agents are required for t-AML development under current understanding of therapy-related leukemias?", "result_summary": "The absence of prior alkylating agent therapy directly contradicts therapy-related AML origin, strongly excluding it as a diagnosis.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.3": "strong_against", "B1.1": "moderate_for", "B1.2": "moderate_against", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 0, "bundle_size": 2, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of prior alkylating agent therapy (E2) and normal renal function (Cr 1.1, E22) strongly support de novo acute myeloid leukemia (AML) as the primary diagnosis, given their direct exclusion of therapy-related AML/t-AML and CML blast crisis as leading differentials?", "result_summary": "The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.1": "moderate_for", "B1.2": "moderate_against", "B1.3": "strong_against", "B2": "moderate_against", "B3": "moderate_against"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 1, "bundle_size": 2, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the lack of documented myeloid lineage markers on peripheral smear (implied by unremarkable physical exam) challenge the diagnosis of de novo AML, which typically presents with detectable myeloid expression (e.g., CD13/CD33) in circulating blasts?", "result_summary": "Absence of myeloid markers in peripheral blood suggests limited evidence for AML detection at this stage but does not definitively exclude the diagnosis due to variable expression patterns.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.1": "weak_against", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 0, "bundle_size": 1, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of 35% blasts with pancytopenia (Hb 10 g/dL, platelets 109,000/mm³) strongly support de novo acute myeloid leukemia (AML), given that this combination is characteristic of acute leukemias over chronic processes?", "result_summary": "The presence of 35% blasts with pancytopenia (anemia/Hb 10 g/dL, thrombocytopenia) supports de novo acute myeloid leukemia (AML) B1.1 as the primary consideration, consistent with acute leukemic presentations."}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.4969199178644764, "B2": 0.024640657084188906, "B3": 0.03080082135523613, "B4": 0.02053388090349076, "B5": 0.02053388090349076, "B1.1": 0.4065708418891171, "B1.2": 0.04517453798767968, "B1.3": 0.04517453798767968}, {"B1": 0.5786817556201256, "B2": 0.009175714941122492, "B3": 0.011469643676403116, "B4": 0.015292858235204158, "B5": 0.015292858235204158, "B1.1": 0.5450374675026763, "B1.2": 0.016822144058724578, "B1.3": 0.016822144058724578}, {"B1": 0.6157421019186813, "B2": 0.002845300985422573, "B3": 0.003556626231778216, "B4": 0.009484336618075245, "B5": 0.009484336618075245, "B1.1": 0.6084391627227633, "B1.2": 0.005216385139941386, "B1.3": 0.0020865540559765546}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No universal instability markers present. Vital signs are stable (BP 122/90 mmHg, pulse 84/min, RR 16/min, O2 saturation 99% on room air). Mild neurologic findings (ataxia, visual acuity decrement) are focal and non-emergent. The hematologic abnormalities (anemia, blasts, thrombocytopenia) while concerning, do not yet indicate imminent multi-organ failure, respiratory decompensation, or uncontrolled hemorrhage requiring stabilization prior to diagnostic assessment.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Root branch B1 (Myeloid Neoplasm) has not yet achieved posterior >=0.75 (0.5787). Dangerous alternative B1.1 (AML, danger=0.9, posterior=0.545) remains unresolved despite exclusion of t-AML/CML blast crisis, requiring further refinement via flow cytometry or bone marrow biopsy. Available discriminators (e.g., lineage markers) could yet change management."}, "turn_budget_used": 4, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.85, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.6084391627227633, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_vignette": "A 57-year-old man presents to the emergency department with several days of malaise, weakness, and night sweats. Today, he experienced a headache with blurry vision, thus prompting his presentation. The patient has a history of diabetes and is followed closely by an endocrinologist. Otherwise, he has lost 10 pounds over the past month. His temperature is 100°F (37.8°C), blood pressure is 122/90 mmHg, pulse is 84/min, respirations are 16/min, and oxygen saturation is 99% on room air. Physical exam is notable for a thin man but is otherwise unremarkable. His visual acuity is 20/100 in both eyes, though he says that he normally has 20/20 vision. His gait is mildly ataxic as well, but his neurological exam is otherwise nonfocal. Laboratory studies are ordered as seen below.\n\nHemoglobin: 10 g/dL\nHematocrit: 31%\nLeukocyte count: 57,500/mm^3 with 35% blasts\nPlatelet count: 109,000/mm^3\n\nSerum:\nNa+: 139 mEq/L\nCl-: 100 mEq/L\nK+: 4.1 Eq/L\nHCO3-: 22 mEq/L\nBUN: 20 mg/dL\nGlucose: 99 mg/dL\nCreatinine: 1.1 mg/dL\nCalcium: 10.0 mEq/L", "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "static_evidence_items": [{"id": "E1", "kind": "direct", "content": "Chief complaint: several days of malaise, weakness, night sweats; today: headache with blurry vision prompting presentation", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E2", "kind": "direct", "content": "Past medical history: diabetes; monitored by endocrinologist", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E3", "kind": "direct", "content": "Weight change: 10-pound weight loss over the past month", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}