n treatment", "Mild fever (99.5°F/37.5°C) with localized skin lesions"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Autoimmune Blistering Disease", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.05310933740417957, "danger": 0.1, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The pressure-resistant plaque morphology strongly argues against typical insect bite presentations while providing borderline support for atypical inflammatory reactions"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Cutaneous Inflammatory Lesions", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.08892157518218899, "posterior": 0.07222869886968424, "danger": 0.05, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Absence of epidermal-dermal interface involvement and intact skin structure reduces likelihood of panniculitis, though fever remains a nonspecific finding for inflammatory or infectious processes"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Systemic symptoms (fever, joint pain)", "Trauma history", "Lesion depth"], "requestable_discriminators": ["MRI for dermis/fat interface", "Skin biopsy for histopathology", "Inflammatory markers (CRP/ESR)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.25, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Reactive Cutaneous Hypersensitivity", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.33012134786387654, "posterior": 0.41450775657214073, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Thick plaque-like morphology is more characteristic of delayed hypersensitivity reactions than typical insect bites."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Medication changes", "Allergen exposures", "T-cell mediated rash patterns"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Skin patch testing", "Drug-specific IgG/IgE testing", "Biopsy for granulomatous vs. lymphocytic infiltrate"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.2, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "pathophysiology"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Vector-Borne/Vector-Related Eczematous Skin Lesions", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.03631560587132111, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of systemic symptoms reduces the probability of drug-induced hypersensitivity but doesn't definitively exclude it."]}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Contact Dermatitis from Plant/Irritant Exposure", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.045319967918233256, "danger": 0.05, "parent": "B2", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Pressure resistance doesn't rule out contact dermatitis but makes it less likely compared to allergic urticarial presentations."]}, "B2.2": {"id": "B2.2", "label": "Drug-Induced Hypersensitivity (Azithromycin Reaction)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.01982748596422704, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "B2", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The analysis of the patient's recent azithromycin use, thick plaque morphology, and clinical context suggests moderate support for drug-induced Type IV hypersensitivity (B3.1) and allergic contact dermatitis from hiking (B3.2), while reducing the likelihood of arthropod bite panniculitis (B3.3) and vector-related diseases (Lyme, Leishmaniasis). Autoimmune blistering disease remains low due to inconsistent lesion features."]}, "B2.3": {"id": "B2.3", "label": "Insect Bite Hypersensitivity", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0070812449872239445, "danger": 0.1, "parent": "B2", "closure_reason": "", "e