nction undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.003556626231778216, "danger": 0.55, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis with Atypical Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.009484336618075245, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Inflammatory/Metabolic Syndrome with Hematologic Mimicry", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.009484336618075245, "danger": 0.25, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.5450374675026763, "posterior": 0.6084391627227633, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The absence of prior alkylating agent therapy directly contradicts therapy-related AML origin, strongly excluding it as a diagnosis.", "The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."], "evidence_against": ["The lack of peripheral myeloid markers on physical exam introduces a small but non-quantitative concern for AML underdiagnosis, but does not decisively weaken its probability.", "Absence of myeloid markers in peripheral blood suggests limited evidence for AML detection at this stage but does not definitively exclude the diagnosis due to variable expression patterns."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of prior haematological disorders (e.g., MDS, MPN, or therapy-related factors)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Flow cytometry for myeloid blast lineage (CD34, CD117, CD13, etc.)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Blast Crisis", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.005216385139941386, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML (t-AML)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0020865540559765546, "danger": 0.65, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of alkylating agents rules out therapy-related AML, and normal renal function undermines classical CML blast crisis criteria. These findings moderately reinforce de novo AML as a diagnostic possibility."]}}, "frontier": ["B1.1", "B1.1"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 5, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the reported history of diabetes without prior alkylating agent exposure contradict likely t-AML causation, as alkylating agents are required for t-AML development under current understanding of therapy-related leu